# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT in this repository
#
# 02AI_drawing_data/   the source corpus. It holds festival visitors' own words,
#                      including 8 records with real names that are redacted at
#                      LOAD time rather than on disk (see emoviz/preprocess_names.py).
#                      Uploading it would transfer identifiable personal data from a
#                      public-engagement event to a third-party host. Keep it local
#                      and back it up somewhere you control.
# RESEARCH PAPERS/     97 copyrighted PDFs. references.bib is tracked instead.
# emoviz/.venv/        1 GB, fully regenerable with `bash emoviz/setup.sh`.
# emoviz/private/      the reviewed name-redaction decision table. It names the tokens it
#                      redacts, so it travels with the dataset, never with the repository.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
02AI_drawing_data/
RESEARCH PAPERS/
!RESEARCH PAPERS/references.bib
!RESEARCH PAPERS/*.md

emoviz/.venv/
emoviz/private/
deck/node_modules/
deck/package-lock.json

# build and scratch artefacts
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc
deck/*slide-*.jpg
deck/*.pdf
!final/*.pdf
emoviz/outputs/app.log
emoviz/outputs/*.prename
emoviz/outputs/*.nodedup
.DS_Store
**/~$*

# LaTeX build artefacts (the PDF itself is tracked)
report/*.bbl
report/*.blg
report/*.lof
report/*.lot
report/*.fls
report/*.fdb_latexmk
report/*.synctex.gz

# regenerable contact sheets of the drawings (human_check.py sample); the coding CSV and sample.json stay tracked
emoviz/outputs/human_check/sheet_*.png
